      "lambda:InvokeFunction on PackagingHandler (2 statements)": "detector-checkpoint-import: TrainingHandler (sync-on-read) and TrainingEventsHandler (SageMaker state change) invoke the Packaging finalize for a Conversion_Record once its job completes (Requirements 7.4, 7.9; packagingHandler.grantInvoke in compute-stack.ts). Scoped to the one PackagingHandler function ARN and its versions/aliases (:*).",
      "servicequotas:GetServiceQuota (2 statements)": "static-camera-video-loop task 10: deployments.py reads the AWS IoT 'Maximum size of a JSON state document' quota and carries it into ShadowManager's shadowDocumentSizeLimitBytes (the device derives its camera report cap from it). Read-only, scoped to the single quota ARN iotcore/L-A295A064 in the stack's own account: the DeploymentsHandler role (single-account Use_Cases) and DDAPortalAccessRole (cross-account Use_Cases).",
      "lambda:InvokeFunction on dda-portal-camera-video-pin": "static-camera-video-loop task 11.4: the Portal_Video_Pin_API pin route hands Video_Validation (up to 60 s of decoding, beyond the API Gateway integration timeout) to its own function as an asynchronous Event invocation. Scoped to the one fixed-name function ARN in this account and region; held by the CameraRegistryHandler role the video function shares.",
      "greengrass:DeleteCoreDevice + IoT thing/certificate removal + device-row cleanup (DevicesRole 4, DDAPortalAccessRole 2)": "device removal (DELETE /devices/{id}, devices.delete_device). DeleteCoreDevice is conditioned on aws:ResourceTag/dda-portal:managed=true; the 7 IoT actions (ListThingPrincipals, ListPrincipalThings, DetachThingPrincipal, UpdateCertificate, DeleteCertificate, ListNamedShadowsForThing, DeleteThing) are scoped to thing/* and cert/*; DynamoDB Query+DeleteItem on the device-registrations table and its indexes, and DeleteItem on dda-portal-account-sync. The removal audits with two PutItem entries (pending, then outcome), so no audit-log Query grant is added.",
      "kms on AccountTablesKey (3 statements)": "security-scan-remediation-high task 8 (R14 DynamoDB; Requirement 14.5; CKV_AWS_119 bcba7f05-bd61-4f0d-a0ac-672b1d990f2c-5 and -6): the customer managed key AccountTablesKey (alias/dda-portal/account-tables, rotation on, retained) encrypts dda-portal-edge-credentials and dda-portal-account-sync. AccountTablesKeyAccess, the policy both tables depend on, grants kms:Decrypt, kms:DescribeKey, kms:Encrypt, kms:ReEncrypt* and kms:GenerateDataKey* on that one key ARN to every principal of the tables: AccountSyncRole, UserAdminRole and DevicesRole, one statement each because the gate counts per principal. grantReadWriteData adds the same grant for AccountSyncRole and UserAdminRole, which the gate counts once."
    },
